# Extrapolate the Impossible: "You may reveal exactly two cards..." - the may is the first card's choice, and choosing
# none is declining (CR 608.2d): nothing is revealed, Bot1 is asked no second card and Bot2 is asked nothing, and both of
# Bot1's cards outside the game stay there. The positive control is
# extrapolate-the-impossible-reveals-two-and-puts-the-opponents-pick-into-hand, where the same choice is taken.

[Bot1 Deck]
Extrapolate the Impossible
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Island
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot1 Sideboard]
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Extrapolate the Impossible.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Choose()
! Bot1.Choose
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Swamp; Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Sideboard = Lightning Bolt; Counterspell
Bot1.Graveyard = Extrapolate the Impossible
Stack.Count = 0
